Why you manually paste JSON now

Because your current setup:

• has no database
• uses only in-memory storage:
  • items = []

--------------------------------------------------

What this means

POST:
• Adds data into RAM (temporary memory)
• Nothing is saved permanently

GET:
• Reads directly from the same in-memory list

--------------------------------------------------

Why you manually send JSON

• There is no frontend application yet
• FastAPI is only exposing API endpoints
• Swagger UI (/docs) acts as your “temporary client”

So right now:
• You are not building an app UI
• You are manually acting as the client

--------------------------------------------------

Key idea

Current architecture:

• Swagger UI = client (manual request tool)
• FastAPI = backend server
• items list = temporary storage (RAM)

--------------------------------------------------

Important behavior

• If server stops:
  • All data is lost

• If server restarts:
  • items = [] again (fresh memory)

--------------------------------------------------

Big picture

JSON input is not “manual work”
• It is how APIs communicate

You are just simulating what a real app would do:
• frontend → sends JSON automatically
• mobile app → sends JSON automatically
• now → you send it manually for learning
